makepad script resources: a packaged build still reads file_resource(<absolute path>) (decision D10f, A33).

A packaged desktop build (MAKEPAD_PACKAGE_DIR set at build time, so `Cx::package_root` is Some) loaded a script
resource from the dependency table, then only from `<package_root>/<dependency path>`, and never from the
filesystem. That is right for a CRATE resource (`crate_resource("makepad_widgets:resources/…")`): its build-tree
path does not exist on another machine and the package carries a copy under its dependency path. It is wrong for a
`file_resource("<absolute path>")`, which has no dependency path at all: the app named a file it wrote or
materialized itself at run time, and packaging never moves it. Such a resource always failed once packaged
("Failed to load resource … (dep: None, packaged: true)"), so every SVG icon the OctosCode module names by its
materialized path (`design::icon_resource`, the lowered kits' icons) drew nothing in the self-contained
OctosCode.app. (Fonts were spared only because the text layer reads a member's path directly before it asks the
resource table, cx_api.rs `get_resource_font_bytes_by_path`.)

Now a resource WITHOUT a dependency path is read from its absolute path in a packaged build too; a crate resource
still loads only from the package (its build-tree path is not read even where it exists), and an unpackaged build
is unchanged. Unit test: a_packaged_build_still_reads_file_resource_from_its_absolute_path.
Applied to every tree by scripts/apply-makepad-patches.sh; tests/a33_packaged_resources.rs checks its shape.
